### [03:29:10 UTC] Step 1 — read_audio/write_audio on synthesized sample
Input: pydub Sine(440), 1000 ms, exported to scratchpad synth_sine.mp3.
Action: Ran scratchpad/step1_rw.py: read_audio(mp3) then write_audio() to both FLAC and WAV; inspected with soundfile.info/read and mutagen.flac.FLAC.
Reasoning: Rules "What to check" step 1 — verify bitrate/sample rate/channels/duration on a controlled signal where ground truth is known.
Output: read_audio OK — sr=44100, 44100 samples, ndim=1 (mono not wrongly reshaped), channels=1, duration=1000 ms, bitrate=63999 bps (in 32k-320k band), dominant freq=440.0 Hz, dtype float64, max_abs=31212.0 (raw int16 PCM scale).
  write_audio FLAC: sr=44100 preserved, channels=1, duration=1.000 s, subtype=PCM_24, flac bitrate=938384 bps (938.4 kbps vs 1058.4 kbps nominal 24-bit PCM), finite=True.
  write_audio WAV: sr=44100, channels=1, duration=1.000 s, PCM_24, 1058.8 kbps.
  BUG: both outputs clipped_fraction=0.99993 and max_abs=1.0, rms=0.99997 (a sine's rms should be ~0.707). write_audio() passes read_audio()'s raw-PCM-scale float64 straight to sf.write with an integer subtype, so every sample |x|>1 is clamped to full scale -> 440 Hz sine becomes a hard-clipped square wave. Production bug in feed.py write_audio(), reported not fixed (source is out of this agent's write scope).

